Original commit body from bdff9381c2164fe34a95fab8e7ed47b544d19bc6:

#1844 had each file-scanning linker claim silence_reason_for_candidates(...)
unconditionally. On compose-go, database-query, subprocess and websocket read
0 files and so reported no_candidate_construct, losing the orchestrator's
more precise no_candidate_files (found by diffing every pass's reason before
and after, not the totals).

The claim now waits for a file to have been read: http, graphql, subprocess,
event-sourcing and database-query use their files_scanned; phoenix-ipc,
argparse-dispatch and go-cobra their files_analyzed. websocket's
files_analyzed counts only files WITH patterns, so it gains files_read.
The symbol-scanning linkers (the original eleven, the FFI bridges) are
unchanged: a construct in the symbol set is looked for whatever files were
read.

test_a_scan_that_read_no_file_keeps_no_candidate_files pins it on a Go-only
repo; making websocket's claim unconditional reds it.

